{"book":10,"chapter":20,"rubric":"LEARNING RUST / THE LANGUAGE IN DEPTH / CHAPTER 20","slides":[{"title":"Lambda and closure","sub":"Chapter 20 · Like Python, but fast","short":"Intro","main":"Closures and iterators compile to an ordinary loop: the abstraction costs nothing.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Python","Rust","No overhead"],"captions":["Python: a one-expression lambda, a list comprehension, and a generator, all interpreted on the fly","Rust: a closure and an adapter chain look similar, but types and ownership are checked at build time","The result compiles to an ordinary loop: the abstraction costs nothing at run time"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["add = lambda a, b: a + b","evens = [x * x for x in v if x % 2 == 0]","total = sum(x for x in evens)"],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":18.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let add = |a, b| a + b;","let total: i32 = v.iter()","    .filter(|x| *x % 2 == 0)","    .map(|x| x * x).sum();"],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":16.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":28.0,"text":"adapter chain","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":154.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":204.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":28.0,"text":"one loop\nin machine code","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":120.0,"text":"speed of a hand loop","tone":"green","size":9.5}]],"cues":[14.6,25.6]}]},{"title":"Closure syntax","sub":"|a, b| a + b","short":"Syntax","main":"Parameters in bars, the body is an expression or a block; types are inferred once.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Parameters in bars","Block, several lines","Types inferred"],"captions":["|a, b| a + b: parameters between vertical bars, then an expression","The body can be a block of any length: a Python lambda cannot do that","Parameter types are inferred from the first use and then stay fixed"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["let inc = |x| x + 1;","inc(5)   // 6"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":20.0,"w":280.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["let describe = |n: i32| {","    let sq = n * n;","    format!(\"{n}² = {sq}\")","};"],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let id = |x| x;","id(5);        // x: i32","id(\"a\");      // error: expected i32"],"hl":[2],"bad":[2],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[15.9,21.4]}]},{"title":"Capturing the environment","sub":"&, &mut, move","short":"Capture","main":"A closure takes variables the weakest way that works; move takes them whole.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["By reference","By mutable ref","move"],"captions":["A closure that only reads a variable takes it by reference; the variable stays with its owner","If a closure changes a variable, it takes &mut, and nobody else can use it while the closure lives","move takes the value whole: the closure can outlive the function or go to another thread"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let k = 3;","let f = |x| x + k;"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":150.0},{"t":"cell","id":"k","x":250.0,"y":40.0,"w":56.0,"h":34.0,"text":"k\n3","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"f","x":250.0,"y":108.0,"w":100.0,"h":40.0,"text":"closure f\n&k →","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":250.0,"y1":88.0,"x2":250.0,"y2":58.0,"tone":"blue","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let mut n = 0;","let mut f = || n += 1;"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":150.0},{"t":"cell","id":"k","x":250.0,"y":40.0,"w":56.0,"h":34.0,"text":"n\n0","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"f","x":250.0,"y":108.0,"w":100.0,"h":40.0,"text":"closure f\n&mut n →","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":250.0,"y1":88.0,"x2":250.0,"y2":58.0,"tone":"red","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let s = String::new();","let f = move || s.len();"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":160.0},{"t":"cell","id":"s","x":250.0,"y":40.0,"w":66.0,"h":34.0,"text":"s\nmoved","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5,"o":0.4},{"t":"cell","id":"f","x":250.0,"y":108.0,"w":120.0,"h":40.0,"text":"closure f\nowns String","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":250.0,"y1":88.0,"x2":250.0,"y2":58.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"dash":"3 3","width":1.6}]],"cues":[16.7,29.1]}]},{"title":"Fn, FnMut, FnOnce","sub":"What a closure does to its environment","short":"Fn","main":"Reads: Fn, changes: FnMut, consumes: FnOnce (one call).","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Fn","FnMut","FnOnce"],"captions":["Fn: only reads the captured values, so it can be called any number of times from many places","FnMut: changes the captured values, many times, but the caller needs mut","FnOnce: consumes the captured values, e.g. returns them, so it can be called once"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Fn\n(reads)","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"FnMut ⊃ Fn\nFnOnce ⊃ FnMut","tone":"muted","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5,"o":0.5},{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":112.0,"lines":["let f = |x| x + k;   // f(1); f(2); f(3)"],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":16.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"FnMut\n(changes)","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":112.0,"lines":["let mut f = |x| { total += x; };","f(1); f(2);   // needs mut"],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":16.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"FnOnce\n(consumes)","tone":"red","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":112.0,"lines":["let f = move || s;   // returns the String","f();  f();   // ✕ cannot call twice"],"hl":[1],"bad":[1],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":16.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[15.9,24.1]}]},{"title":"Passing closures","sub":"Generics, Box<dyn Fn>, fn","short":"Passing","main":"F: Fn is fast; Box<dyn Fn> is mixed; fn takes no capture.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Generic parameter","Box<dyn Fn>","fn pointer"],"captions":["fn apply<F: Fn(i32) -> i32>(f: F, x: i32): a copy per closure, the call is inlined","Box<dyn Fn(i32) -> i32> holds different closures in one list or returns from if branches; the price: an indirect call","The fn(i32) -> i32 pointer captures nothing, like a C function pointer; a closure carries its own context"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["fn apply<F: Fn(i32) -> i32>(f: F, x: i32) -> i32 {","    f(x)","}","apply(|n| n * 2, 21)   // 42"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":17.0,"w":350.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"v","x":70.0,"y":36.0,"w":100.0,"h":24.0,"text":"Vec<Box<dyn Fn>>","tone":"yellow","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":90.0,"w":90.0,"h":26.0,"text":"|x| x + 1","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":90.0,"h":26.0,"text":"|x| x * x","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":290.0,"y":90.0,"w":90.0,"h":26.0,"text":"|x| -x","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":70.0,"y1":48.0,"x2":70.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":90.0,"y1":48.0,"x2":170.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e3","x1":110.0,"y1":48.0,"x2":270.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["fn double(x: i32) -> i32 { x * 2 }","let table: [fn(i32) -> i32; 2] = [double, abs];","table[0](21)   // 42"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":18.0,"w":350.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":128.0,"text":"8 bytes per element, as in C","size":9.0}]],"cues":[17.1,26.2]}]},{"title":"Laziness","sub":"Adapters and consumers","short":"Laziness","main":"Adapters only build a pipeline; a consumer starts the work.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Adapters do nothing","Consumer starts","Like a Python generator"],"captions":["iter().map(...).filter(...) only builds a pipeline struct: no value is computed yet","sum(), collect(), count() are consumers: they pull values one at a time and run the whole chain","The same laziness as Python generators, but with no interpreter and no separate stack frames"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":70.0,"y":60.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"iter","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":170.0,"y":60.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"map","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"filter","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":112.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":118.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"muted","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":212.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":218.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"muted","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"text":"nothing computed yet","tone":"yellow","size":10.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":60.0,"w":72.0,"h":28.0,"text":"iter","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":60.0,"w":72.0,"h":28.0,"text":"map","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":60.0,"w":72.0,"h":28.0,"text":"filter","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":308.0,"y":60.0,"w":72.0,"h":28.0,"text":"sum","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"p","x":50.0,"y":100.0,"w":20.0,"h":20.0,"text":"5","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":80.0,"y1":100.0,"x2":270.0,"y2":100.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":1